ne!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;border-top:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important;margin:0!important;padding:.7rem 0 .75rem!important}main#main .c3-cc tbody tr:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.16)!important}main#main .c3-cc th,main#main .c3-cc td{padding-left:0!important;padding-right:0!important}}main#main figure.c3ph-hero{background:none!important;border:0!important;box-shadow:none!important;border-radius:0!important;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none!important;backdrop-filter:none!important;padding:0!important}main#main figure.c3ph-hero figcaption{padding:0!important}main#main .c3-cc,main#main .c3-gchart,main#main figure.c3ph-hero,main#main figure.rp-calc,main#main .rp-year,main#main .rp-lend,main#main .rp-steps,main#main .rp-req,main#main .rp-fees{max-width:720px!important;box-sizing:border-box}@media (min-width:1100px){main#main .rp-side{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,665px) minmax(0,380px);column-gap:2.5rem;align-items:start}main#main .rp-side.a{grid-template-rows:auto auto auto 1fr}main#main .rp-side.b{grid-template-rows:auto 1fr}main#main .rp-side>*{grid-column:1}main#main .rp-side>figure{grid-column:2;grid-row:1/-1;margin:.3rem 0 1.2rem!important;max-width:none!important;width:100%}}
+</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One large oceanfront Myrtle Beach resort's rental desk took about 4 of every 10 rent dollars, then billed the owner for more. Its written rules set three fees on the gross rent, meaning all the rent guests paid:</p><div class="rp-side a"><ul class="rp-fees" aria-label="The program's three fees on the rent"><li><b>35%</b>management fee</li><li><b>2.6%</b>marketing fee</li><li><b>1%</b>to replace worn items</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It also charged a health club fee of $53 a month plus tax. It billed repairs job by job, and added a handling fee when it paid an outside contractor's bill for the owner. It asked the owner's approval for any single repair over $500, unless the owner could not be reached or an emergency could not wait.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Its sample owner statement shows what was left. In one slow January, the unit rented 3 nights for $229.95. The owner's check was $66.84.</p><figure class="rp-card" role="group" aria-label="A sample owner statement from the resort's rental desk"><p class="k">Owner statement, one January</p><dl><div><dt>Rent for 3 nights</dt><dd>$229.95</dd></div><div><dt>Management fee, 35%</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$80.48</dd></div><div><dt>Marketing fee, 2.6%</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$5.98</dd></div><div class="sub"><dt>After the program's fees</dt><dd>$143.49</dd></div><div><dt>Health club</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$40.85</dd></div><div><dt>Replacing worn items, 1%</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$2.30</dd></div><div><dt>A repair</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$22.50</dd></div><div><dt>The owner's own charges</dt><dd class="m">&minus;$11.00</dd></div><div class="t"><dt>Check to the owner</dt><dd>$66.84</dd></div></dl><figcaption>The rental desk's sample owner statement, redrawn by Chapter3. The owner kept about 29 cents of each rent dollar that month.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The statement's only income line is the room rent for the nights booked. It has no line for the cleaning fees guests pay.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-keeps-more"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Program vs Airbnb">Which keeps more: the program, Airbnb or Vrbo?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Running it yourself on Airbnb or Vrbo keeps more of each booking, before you pay for the work. Airbnb is moving every home host to one fee, and most hosts pay 15.5 percent. Its old 3 percent host fee is being phased out. Vrbo takes 12 percent of the rent and the cleaning fee.</p><figure class="c3-gchart"><div role="table" aria-label="What the owner keeps of each $1,000 of rent, before the cleaner and other costs"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What the owner keeps of each $1,000 of rent, before the cleaner and other costs</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Who rents it, fee</span><span role="columnheader">owner keeps</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Vrbo, run yourself</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Vrbo takes 12%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.88" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$880</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Airbnb, run yourself</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Airbnb takes 15.5%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.845" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$845</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The rental program</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">one resort's desk takes 38.6%</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.614" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$614</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>The program's figure is before its monthly club fee and its repair charges, so the real difference is larger. Airbnb's figure uses the fee most hosts pay. Vrbo's uses its pay-per-booking fee.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The difference, $231 of each $1,000, pays for the work the desk did: the cleaner, linens, supplies and answering guests. If those cost you less, running it yourself keeps more.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Three ways to rent an oceanfront condo</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The way</th><th scope="col">What it keeps</th><th scope="col">Who runs it day to day</th><th scope="col">Who pays the state tax</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">The building's rental program</th><td data-label="What it keeps">38.6% of rent at one resort, plus fees</td><td data-label="Who runs it day to day">The desk books, cleans, answers guests</td><td data-label="Who pays the state tax">The program pays it</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Airbnb or Vrbo, run yourself</th><td data-label="What it keeps">15.5% on Airbnb, 12% on Vrbo</td><td data-label="Who runs it day to day">You, a cleaner and a handyman</td><td data-label="Who pays the state tax">The site pays it on its bookings</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A local vacation rental manager</th><td data-label="What it keeps">A share of the profit, not of the rent</td><td data-label="Who runs it day to day">The manager: guests, taxes, repairs</td><td data-label="Who pays the state tax">The manager pays it when it books</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A local manager is a third way. Full service here covers marketing, guest messages, the books, taxes and repairs. In what we see, managers price it as a share of gross profit, not of the rent. Its percentage cannot be set beside the shares above. What managers here charge is on our <a href="/invest/property-management/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property management page</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The worst mistake we see when owners run it themselves is the cheapest cleaner. Owners who hired one have had theft and damage.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">How does your building's program compare?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the building. We get its program agreement and owner statements and lay one year both ways side by side.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Send us the building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="a-year"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="A year, both ways">What does a year look like both ways?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the bookings of the average Myrtle Beach short-term rental, that desk's terms pay the owner about $6,600 a year less than Airbnb. That is about $550 a month. It has to pay the cleaner and supplies, and the rest is what your time earns.</p><table class="rp-year"><caption>One year on the average short-term rental's bookings</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The year</th><th scope="col">Myrtle Beach</th><th scope="col">North Myrtle Beach</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Bookings in a year</th><td>$25,807</td><td>$34,401</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">The program's terms: less 38.6% and $53 a month</th><td>about $15,200</td><td>about $20,500</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Airbnb: less 15.5%</th><td>about $21,800</td><td>about $29,100</td></tr><tr class="t"><th scope="row">Left to pay the cleaner, supplies and your time</th><td>about $6,600</td><td>about $8,600</td></tr></tbody></table><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The table gives both ways the same bookings. Both also pay the same homeowners association (HOA) fee, property tax, insurance and utilities, so it compares only the fees. This is the average listing, not a promise of income.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The bookings include the cleaning fees guests pay. On Airbnb or Vrbo, you set that fee, and it comes to you with the rent, less the site's fee. The resort desk's statement showed room rent only. The table still counts the cleaning fees on the program side, which favors the program.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Put in your own numbers below. Start with what a cleaner, linens and supplies would cost you in a year, and the hours you would spend each month.</p><figure class="rp-calc" role="group" aria-label="Run your own year: the program against running it yourself"><p class="k">Run your own year</p><div style="display:grid;gap:.75rem"><label>Bookings in a year<span class="u">$ <input id="rpGross" type="number" min="0" step="500" value="25807" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="Bookings in a year"></span></label><label>The program's share<span class="u"><input id="rpShare" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="38.6" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="The program's share"> %</span></label><label>The program's monthly charges<span class="u">$ <input id="rpMonthly" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="53" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="The program's monthly charges"></span></label><label>The booking site's fee<span class="u"><input id="rpFee" type="number" min="0" step="0.1" value="15.5" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="The booking site's fee"> %</span></label><label>Cleaner, linens, supplies, a year<span class="u">$ <input id="rpClean" type="number" min="0" step="100" value="0" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="Cleaner, linens, supplies, a year"></span></label><label>Your hours a month<span class="u"><input id="rpHours" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="0" oninput="c3Rp()" aria-label="Your hours a month"></span></label></div><div class="o"><span>Program pays you</span><strong id="rpProg">$15,209</strong></div><div class="o"><span>Running it yourself pays you</span><strong id="rpSelf">$21,807</strong></div><div class="o big"><span>Difference</span><strong id="rpGap">$6,597</strong></div><p class="v" id="rpSay">Running it yourself keeps $6,597 more before your cleaner and supplies. The bookings already hold the cleaning fees guests pay. Enter what you would pay out, and your hours.</p></figure><script>function c3Rp(){var g=function(id){var e=document.getElementById(id);var v=e?parseFloat(e.value):NaN;return isFinite(v)&&v>0?v:0};var m=function(n){return (n<0?"-":"")+"$"+Math.round(Math.abs(n)).toLocaleString("en-US")};var P=document.getElementById("rpProg"),S=document.getElementById("rpSelf"),D=document.getElementById("rpGap"),Y=document.getElementById("rpSay");if(!P||!S||!D||!Y)return;var gr=g("rpGross"),sh=Math.min(g("rpShare"),100),mo=g("rpMonthly"),fe=Math.min(g("rpFee"),100),cl=g("rpClean"),hr=g("rpHours");var prog=gr*(1-sh/100)-12*mo,self=gr*(1-fe/100)-cl,gap=self-prog;P.textContent=m(prog);S.textContent=m(self);D.textContent=m(gap);if(!gr){Y.textContent="Enter the bookings for a year.";return}if(gap<=0){Y.textContent="The program pays you more at these numbers.";return}Y.textContent=hr>0?"Running it yourself keeps "+m(gap)+" more, about "+m(gap/(hr*12))+" for each hour of your time.":"Running it yourself keeps "+m(gap)+" more"+(cl?"":" before your cleaner and supplies. The bookings already hold the cleaning fees guests pay")+". Enter your hours to see it per hour."}document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",c3Rp);</script><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a full estimate of a self-managed rental, with the taxes by town, use our <a href="/invest/str-tools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental calculator</a>. What rentals here earn is on our <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Airbnb income page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="buildings"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Buildings with programs">Which Myrtle Beach buildings have rental programs?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 8 in 10 condos for sale in Horry County's oceanfront buildings say the unit is in a rental program. That is about 83 percent in Myrtle Beach and about 76 percent in North Myrtle Beach. Every one of the 43 oceanfront buildings with 8 or more condos for sale has units listed in a program.</p><div class="rp-side b"><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:640px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rental-program-vs-airbnb/oceanfront-resort-from-the-beach-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/invest-rental-program-vs-airbnb/oceanfront-resort-from-the-beach-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/invest-rental-program-vs-airbnb/oceanfront-resort-from-the-beach-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 680px) 100vw, 640px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An oceanfront condo resort with rows of balconies, seen from the beach at dusk" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Philip Tellis. License: CC BY-SA 2.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 2.0">Photo: Philip Tellis</a></span></div><figcaption>Grande Shores, an oceanfront condo resort in Myrtle Beach, from the beach. When we counted, all 7 of its condos for sale said they were in a rental program.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Their listings give 159 building names. The chart shows the buildings with 15 or more condos for sale. In 13 of the 43 buildings with 8 or more for sale, every unit for sale says it is in a program.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the other 30, some condos for sale do not say they are in one. That is what the ads say, not the building's rules.</p></div><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=row]{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) auto;column-gap:.8rem;align-items:start}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .b{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .dot{display:none}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list .f{display:block}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-list [role=cell]{justify-content:flex-end}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact c3-gchart-list"><div role="table" aria-label="How many condos for sale in each oceanfront building say they are in a rental program"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">How many condos for sale in each oceanfront building say they are in a rental program</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Building, city</span><span role="columnheader">in a program, of those for sale</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Landmark Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.9" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">75 of 83</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Coral Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.95" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">36 of 38</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Caravelle Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.97" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">36 of 37</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ocean Reef Resort North Tower</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.84" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">26 of 31</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Monterey Bay Suites Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.83" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">24 of 29</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Sand Dunes Phase II</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.93" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">27 of 29</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Bluewater Resort high rise</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.85" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">22 of 26</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Sea Mist Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.72" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18 of 25</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Compass Cove Pinnacle Oceanfront Tower</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 of 25</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beach Cove</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 of 25</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Caribbean Oceanfront Suite Tower</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">25 of 25</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Bay Watch North Tower</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">North Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.91" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21 of 23</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">The Palace</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.82" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">18 of 22</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beach Colony</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.94" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17 of 18</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Grande Cayman Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.94" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">16 of 17</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Meridian Plaza</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.67" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">10 of 15</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Holiday Sands</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">Myrtle Beach</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.87" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">13 of 15</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>All 17 buildings with 15 or more condos for sale, named as their listings name them. One more listing name, &quot;Mb Resort Rt&quot; (21 of 34), is not the name of a building, so it is left out. The chart counts what the listings say, not the building's rules.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Program condos are smaller and cheaper. About half ask $200,000 or less, against about 3 in 10 of the rest. About 4 in 10 have two bedrooms or more, against about 6 in 10 of the rest.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They are also run more like hotel rooms. About 6 in 10 say the HOA fee pays the electric bill, against about a third of the rest. Nearly all are sold furnished.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">What a condo's ad says is not the building's rules. The building's recorded documents say whether its program is required. HOA fees by building are on our <a href="/invest/condo-buildings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">oceanfront condo buildings page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Looking at one of these buildings?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which one. We pull its program terms and run the year both ways for the condo you like.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Ask us about a building</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="leaving"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Leaving the program">Can you leave the program or list on Airbnb too?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not both at once at that resort. Its desk was the owner's only rental agent and collected all the rent. Booking your own guests and keeping the money broke the agreement.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">An owner who booked a guest through the management office earned a referral commission instead, 20 percent of the nightly rate in most months.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Leaving took about three months:</p><ol class="rp-steps" aria-label="How an owner left the resort's rental program"><li>Written notice at least 90 days ahead.</li><li>The desk took out its hotel items, such as the vacuum, linens and towels, and did a final cleaning.</li><li>It turned off the keycard lock and had a locksmith rekey the door, so the unit had its own lock again.</li><li>Any balance was due within 10 days of the final statement.</li></ol><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">After the rekey, the door is yours again. You choose how your own guests get in.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="standards"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What it requires">What does the program make you buy and keep up?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A unit furnished like a hotel room, to the desk's standard, down to the dishes:</p><ul class="rp-req" aria-label="What the program required"><li><b>Locks and phone</b><p>A keycard lock on the resort's key system, and a phone line with voicemail through the phone service the program named.</p></li><li><b>Beds</b><p>A queen sleeper sofa. A king bed in the main bedroom and two queens in each guest room, where they fit.</p></li><li><b>Dishes</b><p>Winter Frost White Corelle plates, Chivalry glasses by Libby and Allison flatware by Rogers.</p></li><li><b>TV</b><p>A flat screen of at least 42 inches in the living room.</p></li><li><b>Updates</b><p>Units were expected to be updated at least once every ten years. A unit came off the program if work rated below standard was not done in time.</p></li><li><b>Insurance</b><p>Liability cover of at least $500,000, carried by the owner.</p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A unit you run yourself has no such list. When we run the numbers on a program unit, we add what its furnishing rules will cost.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want the program's rules read before you sign?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We get the agreement, read the exit, owner-stay and furnishing rules, and tell you what they cost.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us read the agreement</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="own-use"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Your own stays">Can you still use your own condo?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, but in a program you book it like a guest. At that resort, owners booked their own stays through the management office, Monday to Friday, 8 to 5. They were asked to check in at the hotel front desk like any guest. The rules set no cap on owner nights.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Running it yourself, you block your own dates on the calendar.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Either way, the IRS limits your own days. The limit is the greater of 14 days or 10 percent of the days the condo is rented at a fair price. Days your family uses it count too.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Go over the limit, and the IRS counts the condo as a home, which limits a rental loss. More on our <a href="/invest/14-day-rule/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">14-day rule page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="loan"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The loan">Does a rental program change the loan?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For many conventional loans, lenders look at the building, not at whether you join its program. Many conventional loans, the standard mortgages, are not made on any unit in a building run like a hotel. That includes a unit you run on Airbnb yourself.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lenders list what makes a building ineligible. One is rules that make owners rent their units through the building's program, limit when owners may stay, or make owners share rental profit with the manager.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hotel services count as well: registration at a front desk, daily cleaning, a central phone, central keys and limits on decorating. A name that says hotel, motel or resort counts too, unless the word only refers to the building's past use. Marketing as a hotel, resort or investment counts as well.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Four of those hotel services were written into that resort desk's rules:</p><table class="rp-lend"><caption>Hotel services lenders list, and the rental desk's own rules</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">What lenders list</th><th scope="col">The rental desk's rules</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Registration at a front desk</th><td>Owners were asked to check in at the hotel front desk like any guest.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A central key system</th><td>Every unit on the rental program had a keycard lock on the resort's key system.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A central phone service</th><td>Phones ran through the phone service the program named.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Limits on decorating</th><td>A full section of decorating rules, down to the dishes.</td></tr></tbody></table><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In what we see, buildings with a rental program usually do not qualify for standard loans, because so many owners are investors. Lenders call these buildings non-warrantable. That many investors also shows the building is run for renting.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The loans that work there are on our <a href="/invest/condotel-financing/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condotel financing</a> and <a href="/invest/non-warrantable-condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">non-warrantable condos</a> pages.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Will a standard loan work in this building?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the building. We read its documents against the lenders' list before you make an offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us review the building's loan rules</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="taxes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Taxes">Who pays the lodging taxes in each case?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whoever books the stay and takes the payment collects and pays South Carolina's tax on it. That is the state's 5 percent sales tax and 2 percent accommodations tax, the tax on short stays.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Who pays South Carolina's tax on a short stay</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Who books it</th><th scope="col">The state's tax on the stay</th><th scope="col">Your state license</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">The program books the guest</th><td data-label="The state's tax on the stay">The program collects and pays it</td><td data-label="Your state license">None needed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Airbnb or Vrbo books the guest</th><td data-label="The state's tax on the stay">The site pays it on the full booking</td><td data-label="Your state license">None needed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You book the guest yourself</th><td data-label="The state's tax on the stay">You collect and pay it</td><td data-label="Your state license">A state retail license, see below</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The exception: an owner who books guests directly needs no retail license if the condo is rented no more than one week in each calendar quarter. That owner still files and pays the tax once a year.</p><ul class="rp-req" aria-label="Other taxes and licenses on a short stay"><li><b>What else Airbnb collects</b><p>The county's and the cities' taxes on the stay, and the local sales taxes the state collects for them. The host handles any other tax.</p></li><li><b>The county's hospitality fee</b><p>3 percent of the rent outside city limits and 1.5 percent inside. When a manager books the stay, the county tells the owner to make sure the manager pays it.</p></li><li><b>Long stays</b><p>A stay of 90 days or more in a row by the same guest owes no hospitality fee.</p></li><li><b>The city license</b><p>Inside Myrtle Beach city limits, every rental property needs a city business license, short-term or long-term.</p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The totals by town are on our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">accommodations tax page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="license"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who may run it">Who may run a Myrtle Beach rental for you?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You, or someone with a South Carolina real estate license. An owner renting his own condo needs no license.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Anyone paid to list it or rent it out for you must be licensed as a property manager or broker. That covers a paid Airbnb co-host, a helper who lists your condo or arranges its rentals. Chapter3 does not manage rentals.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether you or a manager runs the rental also changes your tax result. How is on our <a href="/invest/str-tax-treatment/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental tax page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="which-fits"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Which fits you">Program or Airbnb: which fits your condo?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The program fits an owner who wants no work, and running it yourself fits an owner who will do the work. About 58 percent of Horry County condo units mail their tax bill outside South Carolina. For an owner who lives out of state, the desk's share pays for someone on site.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Which way fits how you will use the condo</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">If</th><th scope="col">Usually</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">You want no guest calls and live out of state</th><td data-label="Usually">The rental program</td><td data-label="Why">Staff on site book and clean</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You will answer guests and have a cleaner you trust</th><td data-label="Usually">Airbnb or Vrbo, run yourself</td><td data-label="Why">You keep the difference for that work</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You want to stay in the condo often</th><td data-label="Usually">Run it yourself, if the building allows</td><td data-label="Why">Program stays went through the office</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">You need a standard loan</th><td data-label="Usually">A building without hotel-style services</td><td data-label="Why">Hotel services block many standard loans</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">The building requires its program</th><td data-label="Usually">Price it with the share taken out</td><td data-label="Why">Every rental there goes through it</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Whether nightly guests beat a yearly lease is on our <a href="/invest/str-vs-ltr/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term against long-term rental page</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="rental-program-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Rental program FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much do rental programs charge in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One oceanfront resort's rental desk took 38.6 percent of the rent, plus a monthly health club fee and repairs. In its sample statement the owner kept about 29 cents of each rent dollar. Airbnb takes 15.5 percent from most hosts.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does Airbnb still charge hosts 3 percent?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Airbnb's 3 percent host fee is being phased out. Airbnb is moving every home host to one fee, and most hosts pay 15.5 percent. Vrbo charges 12 percent.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I use Airbnb while I am in the program?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not at the resort whose rules this page shows. Its desk was the only rental agent, and booking your own guests broke the agreement. Leaving took 90 days' notice.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who pays the accommodations tax when the program books the guest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The program, because it takes the payment. If you book a guest yourself, you collect and pay that stay's tax.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does joining a rental program affect my loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For many standard loans, the lender looks at the building, not at whether you join. Many standard loans are not made on any unit in a building run like a hotel. Signs are a front desk, central keys or rules on when owners may stay.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I need a license to rent out my own condo?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No real estate license. Anyone paid to list or rent it for you needs one. Inside Myrtle Beach city limits, every rental also needs a city business license.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://homesforsalelistings.net/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/kingston-manual.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Kingston Resorts owner manual, 2017 copy</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/1857" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb host fees</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb taxes in South Carolina</a>, <a href="https://help.vrbo.com/articles/How-is-the-booking-fee-calculated" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vrbo booking fee</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/tax/accommodations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR accommodations tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/treasurer/hospitality-fee/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County hospitality fee</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach business licenses</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t40c057.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 40-57</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lender project rules</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p527" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 527</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/26/1.469-1T" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 CFR 1.469-1T</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/26/1.469-5T" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 CFR 1.469-5T</a>. Program terms: one oceanfront resort's owner manual. Bookings: AirROI, past 12 months, average listing. Buildings: our count of condos for sale in Horry County oceanfront buildings. Not tax or legal advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">An oceanfront condo resort in Myrtle Beach, from the beach. Photo: Philip Tellis, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 2.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Grande_Shores_Resort.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized it to 1200 and 600 px wide WebP files, and cut a wide share image from the middle.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them. Each photo keeps the license listed with it.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-rental-program-vs-airbnb/oceanfront-resort-from-the-beach-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-rental-program-vs-airbnb/oceanfront-resort-from-the-beach-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"An oceanfront condo resort with rows of balconies, seen from the beach at dusk","caption":"Grande Shores, an oceanfront condo resort in Myrtle Beach, from the beach. When we counted, all 7 of its condos for sale said they were in a rental program.","description":"An oceanfront condo resort with rows of balconies, seen from the beach at dusk","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Philip Tellis"},"creditText":"Philip Tellis, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Philip Tellis, CC BY-SA 2.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Grande_Shores_Resort.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Grande_Shores_Resort.jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Grande Shores, Ocean Boulevard, seen from the beach, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Put the program's statement next to an Airbnb year.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send us the listing or the building. We get the agreement and the owner statements, run the year both ways, and show you what you would keep.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us the listing</a></div></section></main>
