 stroke-width="1.1"/><text class="r" y="3.1" text-anchor="middle">17</text></g></g><g><path d="M114.8 246.8L121.8 246.8" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="1.1"/><circle cx="114.8" cy="246.8" r="2.4" fill="#1c2028"/><g transform="translate(194.5 112.2)"><g class="k"><rect x="-110.7" y="15.3" width="221.3" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="-110.7" y="14" width="221.3" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">1</text><text class="l" x="0" y="30" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="0">Apartments, Carolina Forest</tspan></text></g></g><g transform="translate(104.3 48.3)"><g class="k"><rect x="13" y="-9.4" width="187.3" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="13" y="-10.7" width="187.3" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">2</text><text class="l" x="15" y="5.3"><tspan x="15">Apartments, Clear Pond</tspan></text></g></g><g transform="translate(121.8 246.8)"><g class="k"><rect x="-112.7" y="-34.2" width="225.4" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#1c2028" fill-opacity=".1"/><rect x="-112.7" y="-35.5" width="225.4" height="21.5" rx="10" fill="#ffffff" fill-opacity=".9" stroke="#ffffff" stroke-width=".8"/><circle r="11" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#91592b" stroke-width="1.6"/><text class="nm" y="4.5" text-anchor="middle">3</text><text class="l" x="0" y="-19.5" text-anchor="middle"><tspan x="0">Rental homes, US 17 Bypass</tspan></text></g></g></g></svg><figcaption style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.6;margin-top:.6rem">The three rental communities DSTs own in Horry County, each at its parcel's center in the county's parcel file. Their other 8 parcels, commercial and industrial sites and a pump station, are not shown. Map data: U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line; Horry County GIS.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They include two large apartment communities, one near Carolina Forest Boulevard and one in the Clear Pond area, a community of rental homes near the US 17 Bypass, and commercial and industrial sites. Six of the 10 trusts bought in the last two years.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-10-d/invest-strategies-dst/dst-apartments-carolina-forest-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-10-d/invest-strategies-dst/dst-apartments-carolina-forest-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-10-d/invest-strategies-dst/dst-apartments-carolina-forest-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An apartment community from above: large apartment buildings, garages, parking lots and a pool inside an orange outline, with woods to the south and a street of houses to the north" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>An apartment community a DST owns near Carolina Forest Boulevard, from above. The orange line is the trust's parcel.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A DST share would be a share of a property like these. If you own an apartment community or a commercial or industrial building, DST sponsors are among the buyers here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-we-do"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What we do">What does Chapter3 do when you sell a Grand Strand rental for a DST?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Chapter3 sells the rental. DST shares are securities, and Chapter3 does not sell them or advise on them. The DST broker sells the share. Each step of the sale and the exchange, with what our agent does:</p><ol class="c3d-steps" aria-label="The sale and the exchange, step by step"><li><strong>Before you list</strong> You choose a qualified intermediary, the company that will hold the money during the exchange, and start talking to a DST broker. After closing you have only 45 days to name the DST. <span class="we">We price the rental and set the listing date so the closing falls where your plan needs it. If a tenant is in the house, the time left on the lease changes which buyers can take it.</span></li><li><strong>The sale closes</strong> The money goes to your intermediary, not to you. Your 45 and 180 days start that day. <span class="we">We choose a buyer who can close on the date, and give your intermediary and closing attorney the closing figures.</span></li><li><strong>By day 45</strong> You name the DST in writing, and any backups. <span class="we">If you want a rental here as a backup, we find and show you choices before day 45.</span></li><li><strong>By day 180</strong> Your share of the trust is bought. If your tax return for the year of the sale is due before day 180, that due date comes first; an extension on the return moves it later. <span class="we">If the backup rental here is the one you buy, we handle the purchase so it closes in time.</span></li><li><strong>The trust sells</strong> You exchange again, or pay the tax. <span class="we">If the next exchange is a rental on the Grand Strand, we find it.</span></li></ol><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">An owner who was done managing from far away</h3><div class="c3d-callout"><p>An agent at Chapter3 sold a tenant-occupied house for a man who had owned it for 15 years. He was moving to New York to be with his sister. He did not want to manage a rental from that distance, or have anyone else manage it. The lease had eight months left.</p><p>These are his numbers, not a promise. His cash flow was over $1,200 a month. The next owner's would be about half, because the buyer would pay higher taxes and carry a larger loan.</p><p>If no investor came, the plan was to offer the tenant a buyout, so buyers who would live in the house could bid too. The agent marketed the house to our list of investors who accept modest cash flow in an appreciating area. A cash buyer closed 13 days after the listing date.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/sell/net-proceeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">net proceeds calculator</a> shows what the sale leaves you before the exchange.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="dst-questions"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">DST questions</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a DST the same as a 1031 exchange?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. A 1031 exchange is the tax rule. A DST share is one kind of property you can buy with it.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a DST a REIT?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. A REIT is a company, and its owners hold shares in it. A DST share counts, for federal income tax, as owning part of the trust's real estate itself. Because of that, it can go into a 1031 exchange.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How is income from a DST taxed?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For federal income tax, you are treated as owning part of the trust's real estate. Your share of the rent goes on your own return, and you deduct your share of the depreciation.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are you personally liable for a DST's loan?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not in the trust the IRS ruling describes. The trust took over the property's loan, and neither the trust nor any owner is personally liable on it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.irs.gov/irb/2004-33_IRB" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Rev. Rul. 2004-86</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/1031" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 U.S.C. 1031</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/856" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 U.S.C. 856</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/1014" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">26 U.S.C. 1014</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/instructions/i8824" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Form 8824 help</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 409</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc559" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 559</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c006.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Code 12-6-1150</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/resources-small-businesses/capital-raising-building-blocks/accredited-investors" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC accredited investors</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/resources-small-businesses/exempt-offerings/general-solicitation-rule-506c" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC Rule 506(c)</a>, <a href="https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/230.506" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">17 CFR 230.506</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/reports/rule-144-selling-restricted-control-securities" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC Rule 144</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1314152/000131415226000030/jllipt-20251231.htm" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">REIT Form 10-K, 2025</a>, <a href="https://www.finra.org/investors/protect-your-money/check-registration" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FINRA BrokerCheck</a>, <a href="https://www.sec.gov/data-research/sec-markets-data/form-d-data-sets" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SEC Form D data</a>. Our counts: original Form D filings, October 2025 to September 2026, and Horry County parcels. Not legal, tax or investment advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">An apartment community a DST owns near Carolina Forest Boulevard, from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from the NAIP service, adjusted the colors and drew the parcel outline from county data.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/invest-strategies-dst/dst-apartments-carolina-forest-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-10-d/invest-strategies-dst/dst-apartments-carolina-forest-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"An apartment community a DST owns near Carolina Forest Boulevard, from above","caption":"An apartment community a DST owns near Carolina Forest Boulevard, from above. The orange line is the trust's parcel.","description":"An apartment community from above: large apartment buildings, garages, parking lots and a pool inside an orange outline, with woods to the south and a street of houses to the north","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP"},"creditText":"USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP, public domain, via The National Map (USGS)","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (USDA Farm Service Agency, NAIP)","license":"https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/","acquireLicensePage":"https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer","isBasedOn":"https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Carolina Forest Boulevard, Carolina Forest, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"}}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Selling a Grand Strand rental?</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send us the address. We price the rental, time the closing to your 45 and 180 days, and give your intermediary and closing attorney the figures.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Plan my rental sale</a></div></section></main>
