-</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Garden City sits on a strip of land between the Atlantic Ocean and a salt marsh, just south of Surfside Beach. Its beach road, Waccamaw Drive, runs down the strip to Garden City Point at the inlet. Business 17 runs inland of the marsh.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Horry and Georgetown county line crosses the beach about a third of a mile south of the Garden City Pier. Most of Waccamaw Drive is south of the line, in Georgetown County. The county decides your property tax, your rental license and the beach rules.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most addresses use Murrells Inlet and its ZIP code, 29576. A band at the north edge uses Surfside Beach.</p><figure class="c3-gc-fig"><div class="c3-gc-frame"><svg class="c3-gc-map" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 2141" role="img" aria-labelledby="c3-gc-map-t"><title id="c3-gc-map-t">Aerial map of Garden City, South Carolina: the beach road, Waccamaw Drive, lies along the ocean with salt marsh behind it. The Horry and Georgetown county line crosses the beach a little south of the pier, and most of the beach road lies south of it, in Georgetown County, down to Garden City Point at the inlet. Business 17 is inland. Numbers 1 to 5 mark the five parts described below.</title><image href="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-garden-city/garden-city-aerial-1000.webp" x="0" y="0" width="1400" height="2141" preserveAspectRatio="none"/><path d="M1285 -170.6L1301.4 -188.9M1402.7 -307L1466.2 -381M1481.5 -398.9L1482.3 -399.9M1269.2 -152.4L1262.2 -144M1262.2 -144L1254 -134.4M1254 -134.4L1223 -98.9M1223 -98.9L1201 -73.2M1201 -73.2L1146.9 -10.6M1146.9 -10.6L1110 34.2M1110 34.2L1079.6 71.5M1079.6 71.5L1055.9 100M1055.9 1