9.5L250.4 130L253 130.8L255.7 132L258.3 133.6L260.9 135.1L263.5 136.7L266.1 137.9L268.7 138.9L271.3 139.6L273.9 140L276.5 140.3L279.1 140.4L281.7 140.5L284.3 140.2L287 140.2L289.6 140.6L292.2 140.9L294.8 141.2L297.4 141.3L300 141.5" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="224.3" cy="119.2" r="4" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5"/><text class="cl" x="224.3" y="109.2" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a5226">Condo high</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="31.7" fill="#2f6f8f">$375k</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="146.5" fill="#8a5226">$207k</text></svg><figcaption>Zillow's typical value, monthly from January 2019. Houses here means single-family homes.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos also sell far more slowly than houses. At the past year's pace, it would take about a year and a half to sell every condo for sale now.</p><div class="c3-mb-tiles"><div class="c3-mb-tile hot"><span class="big">About 18 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every condo for sale in the city, at the past year's pace</span></div><div class="c3-mb-tile"><span class="big">About 4 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every house and townhouse for sale in the city</span></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That gives a condo buyer room to negotiate. On the house side, there are fewer homes for sale than buyers in a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the past year, condos in the city resold for about $175,000 in the middle: half sold for more, half for less. Houses resold for about $540,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">Is a Myrtle Beach address in the City of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not. About 3 in 4 houses and buildings with a Myrtle Beach mailing address are outside the city limits. Outside the city, the county's rental rules apply, not the city's.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest and Forestbrook are almost all outside the city, and Socastee is entirely outside it. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers that area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is a separate city. A short-term rental there needs a business license, and for now there is no special zoning or permit process beyond it. Our <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Tax and flood insurance">What do property tax and flood insurance cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a second home or rental pays almost four times the property tax of a home you live in. You apply for the lower rate on the home you live in, and our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> shows how.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Property tax each year inside the City of Myrtle Beach</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The home</th><th scope="col">A home you live in</th><th scope="col">A second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Every $100,000 of value</th><td data-label="A home you live in">$404</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">$1,528</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $540,000 house</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $2,180</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $8,250</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $175,000 condo</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $710</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $2,670</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Will you need flood insurance?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For most houses, no. Only about 1 in 23 houses in the city is in the high-risk flood zone of FEMA, the Federal Emergency Management Agency. About 1 in 4 condos is, many of them at the ocean's edge.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the high-risk zone, your lender will require flood insurance. On a house there, it usually costs about $800 a year. Outside that zone, federal rules do not require it, and a policy usually costs about $600.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo's HOA insures the building itself and adds the cost to the HOA fee.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the tax and the flood zone for one address</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the address. We work out its property tax as your main home and as a second home, and look up its flood zone.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work out a home's tax and flood zone</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the house neighborhoods, the beach and the price of a condo. The hard ones are the condo market, the season and the flood zone at the ocean.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The house neighborhoods are mostly owners' main homes.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The beach, the Boardwalk, golf, a large hospital and the airport are all inside the city.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Condos cost far less than houses, a way to own at the beach for less.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>More people live in the city every year.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Condo prices are falling, and condos take far longer to sell than houses. <span class="c3-pc-do">We help you pick the building and negotiate the price.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Rental income comes mostly in summer. <span class="c3-pc-do">We plan the year with you before you buy.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Many oceanfront condos are in the high-risk flood zone. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the flood zone and the building's insurance for you.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Most houses cannot be rented by the night. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the zone of any address you send us.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="myrtle-beach-real-estate-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach real estate FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you do short-term rentals in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, only in the zones where the city allows them, which hold most condos and almost no houses. The city bans rentals under 90 days in every zone for homes, except one zone set aside for visitor stays.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's market?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For condos, yes: there are about 18 months of condos for sale, and prices are falling. For houses, no: there are about 4 months of houses for sale.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Carolina Forest in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Carolina Forest has a Myrtle Beach address, but only about 1 in 75 houses and buildings in its ZIP code, 29579, is inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax on a second home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $1,528 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value inside the city. A home you live in pays about $404.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the difference between Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach are two separate cities with different rental rules. Myrtle Beach allows nightly rentals only in some zones. North Myrtle Beach, for now, asks only for a business license, with no special zoning or permit process beyond it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R1468.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city rentals</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city licenses</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R729.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">air base</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R986.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Boardwalk</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/photos_of_the_week/pow090420.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grand Park</a>, <a href="https://grandedunescommunities.sites.townsq.io/2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grande Dunes</a>, <a href="https://marketcommonmb.com/parks-playgrounds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Market Common</a>, <a href="https://pinelakes.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pine Lakes</a>, <a href="https://www.thedunesclub.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dunes Club</a>, <a href="https://www.mygrandstrandhealth.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hospital</a>, <a href="https://www.flymyrtlebeach.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">airport</a>, <a href="https://selling-guide.fanniemae.com/sel/b4-2.1-03/ineligible-projects" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fannie Mae</a>, <a href="https://www.airbnb.com/help/article/2328" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airbnb taxes</a>, <a href="https://www.fema.gov/openfema-data-page/fima-nfip-redacted-policies-v2" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">flood policies</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census</a>, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/cew/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA maps</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tax levy</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NMB rentals</a>. Counts are ours, from city zoning, county parcels, FEMA and deeds. Listings in aggregate from CCMLS. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses and condo towers on the same beach in Myrtle Beach. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops.</div><div role="listitem">Oceanfront condo towers south of dow