-</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city has eight parts a buyer can tell apart, and each gives you something the others do not. Five run along the ocean; the other three lie inland. The numbers on the map match the entries below.</p><figure class="c3-nmb-fig"><div class="c3-nmb-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/north-myrtle-beach-parts-map.svg" width="760" height="418" alt="Map of the eight parts of North Myrtle Beach, numbered 1 to 8: Cherry Grove, Little River Neck, Tilghman Beach, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach, Windy Hill, west of US 17 and across the waterway, and the separate town of Atlantic Beach." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ol class="c3-nmb-key" aria-label="The eight parts of North Myrtle Beach"><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#2f6f8f" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#cherry-grove">Cherry Grove</a>: a boat behind the house on the channels</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#5f8a4e" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#little-river-neck">Little River Neck</a>: houses north of the marsh, most of them main homes</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#8a5a9e" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#tilghman-beach">Tilghman Beach</a>: houses by the ocean, most of them main homes</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#c4783a" data-n="4" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#ocean-drive">Ocean Drive</a>: Main Street and a maritime forest</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#b4553f" data-n="5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#crescent-beach">Crescent Beach</a>: a house near the ocean for less</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#a07a2a" data-n="6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#windy-hill">Windy Hill</a>: beach houses under the trees, south of Atlantic Beach</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#5c6b78" data-n="7" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#west-of-us-17">West of US 17</a>: newer houses a few minutes from the beach</span></li><li><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#3f7f74" data-n="8" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><a href="#across-the-waterway">Across the waterway</a>: golf, newer houses and almost no flood zone</span></li></ol><p style="margin:.7rem 0 0">We drew these parts from the county's records and its maps of the old beach towns' lots, so the lines between them are approximate. The grey patch is the town of Atlantic Beach, the blue line is the Intracoastal Waterway, and the brown line is US 17. Map data: Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.</p></figcaption></figure><h3 id="cherry-grove" data-toc="Cherry Grove" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#2f6f8f" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Cherry Grove: a boat behind the house</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cherry Grove is the part for a boat at the back door. Channels were dug into its marsh in the 1970s, and about 680 houses now back onto them or the marsh edge. Many have a dock behind the house.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-channels-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="Cherry Grove from above: rows of houses on narrow lots between dug channels, with docks behind them, the marsh beyond, and the ocean along the bottom, labelled Boat ramp, Heritage Shores, Channel houses and Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Cherry Grove from above, 2023 aerial: houses on the dug channels, many with a dock behind them, the marsh, the boat ramp and Heritage Shores.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city's boat ramp is on the Cherry Grove marsh, and boats reach the ocean through Hog Inlet. Heritage Shores Nature Preserve has walking paths on an island in the marsh, and the Russell Burgess Coastal Preserve has a boardwalk.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cherry Grove Pier stands here, in the city's northernmost beach section. A house on the channels resold for about $715,000 at the middle (38 sales), and elsewhere in Cherry Grove about $665,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The trade-off is flood insurance: almost every house here is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, channel houses included. Only about 1 in 4 houses is the owner's main home.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Cherry%20Grove">Send me homes in Cherry Grove<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="little-river-neck" data-toc="Little River Neck" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#5f8a4e" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Little River Neck: houses north of the marsh</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River Neck suits a buyer who wants a house among owners who live there. It lies north of the Cherry Grove marsh, along Little River Neck Road.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tidewater Plantation is its largest neighborhood, and about 8 in 10 of its houses are the owner's main home. Builders are still selling new houses here: 53 in the past year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Neck also holds most of the city's manufactured homes, about 660 of 800.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Little%20River%20Neck">Send me homes in Little River Neck<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="tilghman-beach" data-toc="Tilghman Beach" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#8a5a9e" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Tilghman Beach: houses by the ocean, most of them main homes</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tilghman Beach suits a buyer who wants a house by the ocean among owners who make it their main home. About 2 in 3 houses here are, the most of any beach part.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/tilghman-beach-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: houses around lakes labelled Tilghman Beach, a row of houses along the beach, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Tilghman Beach from above, 2023 aerial: a row of houses along the ocean, and streets of houses around the lakes behind them.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It grew from one large tract that Charles T. Tilghman Jr. developed in 1948. Its houses sell for the most of any part.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Tilghman Estates, its largest neighborhood, the middle of 19 house resales was about $1.05 million. Seabrook Plantation resold for about $750,000, the middle of 9 sales.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of its homes in the flood zone are condos, not houses.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Tilghman%20Beach">Send me homes in Tilghman Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="ocean-drive" data-toc="Ocean Drive" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#c4783a" data-n="4" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Ocean Drive: Main Street and a maritime forest</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ocean Drive is the part with Main Street, which runs back from the ocean. McLean Park, built around a small lake, is about a 5-minute walk from it.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-main-street-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="Ocean Drive from above: Main Street running back from the beach, a park with a small lake labelled McLean Park, condo towers along the beach and the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Ocean Drive from above, 2023 aerial: Main Street running back from the beach, McLean Park and its lake, and the condo towers along the ocean.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The shag is South Carolina's state dance. In the old beach towns of Ocean Drive and Crescent Beach, a pavilion and amusement park drew crowds to dance it.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/ocean-drive-beach-pavilion-postcard-1941-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="755" alt="A postcard of a long wooden pavilion on the beach at Ocean Drive, with Roberts Pavilion and Dancing painted on its end wall and old cars parked beside it" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-US-no_notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Postcard, 1941, public domain. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Postcard, 1941, public domain</a></span></div><figcaption>The pavilion at Ocean Drive Beach on a 1941 postcard, with &quot;Dancing&quot; painted on its end wall.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve, which the city calls its last maritime forest, has dunes 30 feet tall and a half-mile trail. Houses in the Ingram Beach neighborhood resold for about $1.35 million at the middle (12 sales).</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Prices here spread wide: the middle half of house resales ran from about $385,000 to $980,000. Most of its homes in the flood zone are oceanfront condos; about 1 in 10 houses is in it.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Ocean%20Drive">Send me homes in Ocean Drive<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="crescent-beach" data-toc="Crescent Beach" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#b4553f" data-n="5" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Crescent Beach: a house near the ocean for less</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Crescent Beach suits a buyer who wants a house near the ocean at a lower price. Its houses resold for the least of the beach parts, and only about 1 house in 100 is in the flood zone, the fewest of the beach parts.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses on the original Crescent Beach lots resold for more. The county records those lots under two names, and their middle prices were about $665,000 and $718,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 18th and Edge pocket park is its own small green space. Crescent Beach ends at Atlantic Beach, a separate town that did not join the city.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/atlantic-beach-between-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: a small town outlined in brass and labelled Atlantic Beach, running from the highway to the ocean, with streets labelled Crescent Beach on one side and Windy Hill on the other" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Atlantic Beach, outlined, is a separate town between Crescent Beach and Windy Hill, from US 17 to the ocean (2023 aerial).</figcaption></figure><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Crescent%20Beach">Send me homes in Crescent Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="windy-hill" data-toc="Windy Hill" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#a07a2a" data-n="6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Windy Hill: beach houses south of Atlantic Beach</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Windy Hill suits a buyer who wants a beach house at one of the lower prices by the ocean. Investors from Conway built it up after World War II.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/windy-hill-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: streets of houses among trees labelled Windy Hill, a row of condo buildings along the beach, and the Atlantic Ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Windy Hill from above, 2023 aerial: streets of houses under the trees, condo buildings along the ocean, and a marsh creek at the left.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses on the original Windy Hill Beach lots resold for about $439,000 at the middle (10 sales). Most of its houses are outside the flood zone; most of its condos are in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yow Park and the 41st Avenue South pocket park are its neighborhood parks.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Windy%20Hill">Send me homes in Windy Hill<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="west-of-us-17" data-toc="West of US 17" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#5c6b78" data-n="7" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>West of US 17: newer houses a few minutes from the beach</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">West of US 17 suits a buyer who wants a newer house close to the beach, with little flood zone. From a typical house here, the drive to Ocean Boulevard is about 4 minutes.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/west-of-us-17-new-streets-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: new streets and ponds cleared for houses labelled West of US 17, ball fields labelled Central Park, and the highway labelled US 17" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>West of US 17 from above, 2023 aerial: new streets cleared for houses, Central Park's ball fields, and US 17.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders sold 94 new houses here in the past year, and the city's 20-acre Central Park is in this part. Chestnut Greens is the largest neighborhood, and its houses resold for about $515,000 at the middle.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sunset Harbour resold for about $760,000 (9 sales), but 68 of its homes are in the high-risk flood zone. Condos here cost the least in the city, about $175,000 at the middle.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=West%20of%20US%2017">Send me homes west of US 17<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="across-the-waterway" data-toc="Across the waterway" class="c3-nmb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-nmb-num" style="background:#3f7f74" data-n="8" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Across the waterway: golf, newer houses and almost no flood zone</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Across the Intracoastal Waterway suits a buyer who wants golf, a newer house and almost no flood zone: 2 homes of about 5,200 are in it. More of the city's new houses sold here than anywhere else.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Barefoot Resort has four golf courses, designed by Greg Norman, Davis Love III, Tom Fazio and Pete Dye. Seven holes of the Norman course run along the waterway.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/barefoot-landing-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="857" alt="From above: shops around a lake labelled Barefoot Landing, the wide Intracoastal Waterway with a marina on its far bank labelled Across the waterway, and US 17" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Barefoot Landing on the Intracoastal Waterway at US 17, 2023 aerial, with the neighborhoods across the waterway on the far bank.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Barefoot Landing, the shops and restaurants on the waterway at US 17, is about 11 minutes by car from Main Street. From a typical house here, the drive to Ocean Boulevard is about 11 minutes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses in Grande Dunes North resold for about $374,000 at the middle, and in Waterside for about $385,000. We pull the HOA papers and fees for any house here.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Across%20the%20waterway">Send me homes across the waterway<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The eight parts side by side</h3><div class="c3-nmb-parts"><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>The eight parts side by side: middle sale prices over the past year, from county deeds</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Typical resold house</th><th scope="col">Typical condo</th><th scope="col">Main homes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#cherry-grove" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Cherry Grove</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $695,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $310,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#little-river-neck" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Little River Neck</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $590,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $320,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#tilghman-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Tilghman Beach</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $725,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $325,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 2 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#ocean-drive" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Ocean Drive</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $600,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $360,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 4 in 10</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#crescent-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Crescent Beach</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $410,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $340,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#windy-hill" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Windy Hill</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $460,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $360,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 1 in 3</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#west-of-us-17" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">West of US 17</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $475,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $175,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="#across-the-waterway" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;text-decoration-thickness:1px">Across the waterway</a></th><td data-label="Typical resold house">About $480,000</td><td data-label="Typical condo">About $275,000</td><td data-label="Main homes">About 3 in 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The last column shows how many houses are the owner's main home. Where that share is low, more houses are second homes or rentals, and fewer people live there all year.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="living-here"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Living here">What is North Myrtle Beach like to live in?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach has about nine miles of ocean beach, running south-west from Hog Inlet. Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive, Crescent Beach and Windy Hill voted to become one city in 1968.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-north-myrtle-beach/cherry-grove-from-above-2012-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Looking up the beach in Cherry Grove from a height: low beach houses and mid-rise condo buildings along the road, the marsh behind them, and a long fishing pier reaching into the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Melikamp. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Melikamp</a></span></div><figcaption>Cherry Grove from a height in 2012: older low beach houses beside mid-rise condos, the marsh behind them, and Cherry Grove Pier.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the 1970s, condo and hotel towers began replacing houses on the oceanfront. Today condos outnumber houses about 3 to 2.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 18,800 people lived in the city at the 2020 Census, about 37 percent more than in 2010. Close to half its homes were kept for seasonal or vacation use. Our <a href="/submarkets/little-river/#living-here" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Little River guide</a> compares that share with the towns nearby.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How is North Myrtle Beach different from Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is not part of Myrtle Beach. It is a separate city in Horry County, with its own city tax and its own rules for nightly rentals. The Myrtle Beach oceanfront, at the SkyWheel, is about 30 minutes south by car without traffic.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The map shows the drives from Main Street to the pier, McLeod Seacoast hospital and Barefoot Landing. The airport is about 35 minutes away and Grand Strand Medical Center about 20. Summer traffic on US 17 makes those drives longer.</p><figure class="c3-nmb-fig" style="max-width:560px"><div class="c3-nmb-frame"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-main-street" viewBox="0 0 360 314" width="360" height="314" role="img" aria-label="Map of North Myrtle Beach: from Main Street, Cherry Grove Pier is about 8 minutes by car, McLeod Seacoast hospital about 9 minutes and Barefoot Landing about 11 minutes." style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:760px;background:#f7f3ec;border:1px solid rgba(28,32,40,.15)"><style>#c3r-main-street text{font-family:'DM Sans',system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;paint-order:stroke;stroke:#f7f3ec;stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round;fill:#1c2028}#c3r-main-s